 "verdict": "INDEPENDENT-ASTROMETRY REPLICATION: the zero-Warsaw-lineage two-leg refit concords with the catalogue per-comet rotations (rho=0.998) and retains the registered inbound-leg in-cap carrier on identical members (refit p=0.037 vs catalogue p=0.0287; CODE-overlap p=0.00688; leg-vs-osculating inbound p=0.0026 against outbound p=0.579).  The carrier is leg-specific on the independent fits, so the anomaly lives in the shared astrometric record rather than in the Warsaw fit products.  Shared astrometry, common dynamics, nuisance absorption and covariance bound interpretation; they do not produce the carrier.",
